### Description

we are noticed that in case if error occurs during tool calls , calling 
```
    stop,
    sendMessage,
    regenerate,
    addToolResult,
    clearError,
    error,
    resumeStream,
  } = useChat<AgentUIMessage>({
    id: storeConversationId,
    sendAutomaticallyWhen:
      lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithToolCalls,
```
will cause infinite recursive loop with ```error``` being undefined.

current workaround to use `lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithToolCallsAndNoError` in place of `lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithToolCalls`
```
function lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithToolCallsAndNoError(options: {
  messages: UIMessage[];
}): boolean {
  return (
    //@ts-ignore
    (this.status as ChatStatus) !== "error" &&
    lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithToolCalls(options)
  );
}
```

